IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Commercial Arbitration Act 2012 (Western Australia) -- is my arbitration agreement binding, must the court send my
-- dispute to arbitration, who appoints the arbitrator, am I being heard, and can the award be set aside, appealed or
-- enforced?
--
-- SEAT: a party to a domestic commercial arbitration, or to a dispute mediated by an arbitrator under s 27D (Daniel's
-- client in 2029; Daniel's company Jarrah in 2035). Every decision is phrased as that party would ask it, from facts the
-- party could state. Where the Act speaks to the court or the arbitral tribunal (ss 8, 11, 18, 24, 31, 34, 34A, 35, 36),
-- the encoding says what it means for the party: what the court must do on the party's request, what the party must be
-- given, and by when the party must act. Judgments the Act hands to the Court ("unless it finds", "the Court finds",
-- "the Court ... is satisfied") are INPUTS, never guessed.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 1(1)-(3) (domestic commercial arbitration; where the Act applies), s 7 (definition and form of
-- arbitration agreement), s 8(1) (referral to arbitration), s 10 (number of arbitrators), s 11(2)-(4) (appointment),
-- s 12(3), (4), (6) (challenge), s 18 (equal treatment; reasonable opportunity), s 24(2)-(5) (hearings and
-- communications), s 27D(1), (4)-(6) (arbitrator as mediator), s 30 (settlement; award on agreed terms), s 31(3)
-- (reasons), s 33(1)(a) (correction within 30 days), s 34(1)-(3) (setting aside; 3 months), s 34A(1), (3), (6) (appeal on
-- a question of law by agreement and leave), s 35(1)-(2) and s 36(1) (recognition and enforcement).
--
-- Edition: the compilation published on legislation.wa.gov.au (mrdoc 45283), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_45283.txt (retrieved 2026-09-07). The deposit names no compilation number; its
-- compilation table ends with the Legal Profession Uniform Law Application Act 2022 Pt 17 Div 5 (in force 1 July 2022).
-- The Act was in force (other than s 45(2) Table items 1 and 4) from 7 August 2013. It has no regulations that set
-- numbers; its numbers are in the text: one arbitrator by default (s 10(2)), 30 days (ss 11(3)(a), 33(1)), 3 months
-- (ss 34(3), 34A(6)).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: Part 1A and ss 2A-6 (interpretation, waiver, court intervention, which court); s 9 and Part 4A (interim
-- measures); ss 12(1)-(2), 13-15 (disclosure duty, challenge procedure, substitution) beyond the s 27D(6) consequence;
-- s 16 (jurisdiction); ss 19-23, 24A, 24B, 25-27C (procedure, representation, default, evidence, subpoenas,
-- consolidation); ss 27E-27J (confidentiality, preliminary point of law); ss 28-29, 32, 33(2)-(8), 33A-33F (substance,
-- termination, specific performance, costs, interest); s 34(4), s 34A(4)-(11) (court powers on setting aside and
-- appeal); s 36(2); Parts 9-11 (miscellaneous, transitional, repeal). Daniel's 2029 conditional costs agreement with a
-- 25% uplift is governed by the Legal Profession Uniform Law (WA) ss 181-183, not this Act; s 33C applies only Part 4.3
-- Division 7 of that Law to the assessment of costs under s 33B(5), and is not encoded. A settlement reached outside
-- arbitral proceedings is a contract (or deed) at general law; this Act does not enforce it, and the encoding says only
-- that.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Commercial Arbitration Act 2012 (WA)`

§§ `numbers the Act sets`

-- s 10(2): "Failing such determination, the number of arbitrators is to be one."
`the default number of arbitrators` MEANS 1

-- s 11(3)(a): "within 30 days of receipt of a request"; "within 30 days of their appointment".
`the appointment period in days` MEANS 30

-- s 33(1): "Within 30 days of receipt of the award, unless another period of time has been agreed on by the parties".
`the correction period in days` MEANS 30

-- s 34(3), s 34A(6): "after 3 months have elapsed".
`the recourse period in months` MEANS 3

§§ `date helpers`

-- A date as the number YYYYMMDD, so that dates in the same calendar order compare in order.
GIVEN `d` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`as a calendar number` MEANS
    DATE_YEAR `d` TIMES 10000 PLUS DATE_MONTH `d` TIMES 100 PLUS DATE_DAY `d`

-- The same day of the month 3 months on, as a calendar number. Where that month has no such day (30 November -> "30
-- February"), the number still sorts after the last real day of the month and before the 1st of the next, so the period
-- ends with the month (INFERENCE: the Interpretation Act 1984 rule for months, not read in this deposit).
GIVEN `d` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`three months on` MEANS
    IF   DATE_MONTH `d` PLUS `the recourse period in months` GREATER THAN 12
    THEN (DATE_YEAR `d` PLUS 1) TIMES 10000 PLUS (DATE_MONTH `d` PLUS `the recourse period in months` MINUS 12) TIMES 100 PLUS DATE_DAY `d`
    ELSE DATE_YEAR `d` TIMES 10000 PLUS (DATE_MONTH `d` PLUS `the recourse period in months`) TIMES 100 PLUS DATE_DAY `d`

-- s 34(3), s 34A(6): the period runs "from the date on which the party ... had received the award or, if a request had
-- been made under section 33, from the date on which that request had been disposed of by the arbitral tribunal".
-- "may not be made after 3 months have elapsed": an application ON the day 3 months on is read as in time (INFERENCE).
GIVEN `the date I received the award` IS A DATE
      `a section 33 request was made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the tribunal disposed of it` IS A DATE
      `the date I apply` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `within 3 months of the award` IF
    IF   `a section 33 request was made`
    THEN `as a calendar number` `the date I apply` AT MOST `three months on` `the date the tribunal disposed of it`
    ELSE `as a calendar number` `the date I apply` AT MOST `three months on` `the date I received the award`

§§ `1, 7 -- is my arbitration agreement binding`

-- s 7(1): "An arbitration agreement is an agreement by the parties to submit to arbitration all or certain disputes which
-- have arisen or which may arise between them in respect of a defined legal relationship, whether contractual or not."
-- s 7(2): "may be in the form of an arbitration clause in a contract or in the form of a separate agreement."
-- s 7(3): "The arbitration agreement must be in writing."
-- s 7(4): "in writing if its content is recorded in any form, whether or not the arbitration agreement or contract has been
-- concluded orally, by conduct, or by other means."
-- s 7(5): met "by an electronic communication if the information contained in it is accessible so as to be useable for
-- subsequent reference."
-- s 7(7): "contained in an exchange of statements of claim and defence in which the existence of an agreement is alleged by
-- one party and not denied by the other."
-- s 7(8): "The reference in a contract to any document containing an arbitration clause constitutes an arbitration
-- agreement in writing, provided that the reference is such as to make that clause part of the contract."
-- s 1(3): "An arbitration is domestic if -- (a) the parties ... have, at the time of the conclusion of that agreement, their
-- places of business in Australia; and (b) the parties have (whether in the arbitration agreement or in any other document
-- in writing) agreed that any dispute ... is to be settled by arbitration; and (c) it is not an arbitration to which the
-- Model Law (as given effect by the International Arbitration Act 1974 (Commonwealth)) applies."
-- "commercial" is not defined in the Act; the Model Law note to s 1 says it "should be given a wide interpretation". It is
-- asked as a fact.
DECLARE `My arbitration agreement` HAS
    `we agreed to arbitrate disputes about a defined legal relationship`        IS A BOOLEAN -- s 7(1)
    `its content is recorded in some form`                                      IS A BOOLEAN -- s 7(4)
    `it is in an electronic communication usable for later reference`           IS A BOOLEAN -- s 7(5)
    `it was alleged in a statement of claim and not denied in the defence`      IS A BOOLEAN -- s 7(7)
    `our contract refers to a document whose arbitration clause it makes part of the contract` IS A BOOLEAN -- s 7(8)
    `both parties had their places of business in Australia when it was made`   IS A BOOLEAN -- s 1(3)(a), (4)
    `the relationship is commercial`                                            IS A BOOLEAN -- s 1(1); borrowed term
    `the Model Law applies under the International Arbitration Act 1974`        IS A BOOLEAN -- s 1(3)(c)
    `the place of arbitration is in Western Australia`                          IS A BOOLEAN -- s 1(2)

@export Is my arbitration agreement in writing (Commercial Arbitration Act 2012 (WA) s 7(3)-(8))?
GIVEN `the agreement` IS A `My arbitration agreement` @desc How your agreement to arbitrate was made and recorded
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my arbitration agreement in writing` IF
        `the agreement`'s `its content is recorded in some form`
    OR  `the agreement`'s `it is in an electronic communication usable for later reference`
    OR  `the agreement`'s `it was alleged in a statement of claim and not denied in the defence`
    OR  `the agreement`'s `our contract refers to a document whose arbitration clause it makes part of the contract`

@export Do I have an arbitration agreement the Act recognises (s 7)?
GIVEN `the agreement` IS A `My arbitration agreement` @desc How your agreement to arbitrate was made and recorded
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have an arbitration agreement` IF
        `the agreement`'s `we agreed to arbitrate disputes about a defined legal relationship`
    AND `Is my arbitration agreement in writing` `the agreement`

@export Is my arbitration a domestic commercial arbitration under the Act (s 1(1), (3))?
GIVEN `the agreement` IS A `My arbitration agreement` @desc How your agreement to arbitrate was made and recorded
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my arbitration a domestic commercial arbitration` IF
        `Do I have an arbitration agreement` `the agreement`
    AND `the agreement`'s `both parties had their places of business in Australia when it was made`
    AND `the agreement`'s `the relationship is commercial`
    AND (NOT `the agreement`'s `the Model Law applies under the International Arbitration Act 1974`)

-- s 1(2): "The provisions of this Act, except sections 8, 9, 17H, 17I, 17J, 35 and 36, apply only if the place of
-- arbitration is in Western Australia."
DECLARE `How much of the Act applies` IS ONE OF
    `the whole Act`
    `only sections 8, 9, 17H to 17J, 35 and 36`
    `not this Act`

@export How much of the Commercial Arbitration Act 2012 (WA) applies to my arbitration (s 1)?
GIVEN `the agreement` IS A `My arbitration agreement` @desc How your agreement to arbitrate was made and recorded
GIVETH A `How much of the Act applies`
DECIDE `How much of the Act applies to my arbitration` IS
    IF      NOT `Is my arbitration a domestic commercial arbitration` `the agreement`
    THEN    `not this Act`
    ELSE IF `the agreement`'s `the place of arbitration is in Western Australia`
         THEN `the whole Act`
         ELSE `only sections 8, 9, 17H to 17J, 35 and 36`

§§ `8 -- must the court send my dispute to arbitration`

-- s 8(1): "A court before which an action is brought in a matter which is the subject of an arbitration agreement must, if a
-- party so requests not later than when submitting the party's first statement on the substance of the dispute, refer the
-- parties to arbitration unless it finds that the agreement is null and void, inoperative or incapable of being performed."
-- s 8(2): arbitral proceedings "may nevertheless be commenced or continued, and an award may be made, while the issue is
-- pending before the court."
@export Must the court refer my dispute to arbitration (s 8(1))?
GIVEN `the agreement` IS A `My arbitration agreement` @desc Your agreement to arbitrate
      `the court action is in a matter the agreement covers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court case is about a dispute your arbitration agreement covers
      `a party asked for referral no later than its first statement on the substance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a party asked the court to refer the dispute before or with its first statement on the merits
      `the court finds the agreement null and void, inoperative or incapable of being performed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The court's finding about the agreement (asked, not guessed)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the court refer my dispute to arbitration` IF
        `Is my arbitration a domestic commercial arbitration` `the agreement`
    AND `the court action is in a matter the agreement covers`
    AND `a party asked for referral no later than its first statement on the substance`
    AND (NOT `the court finds the agreement null and void, inoperative or incapable of being performed`)

§§ `10, 11 -- who appoints the arbitrator`

-- s 10: "(1) The parties are free to determine the number of arbitrators. (2) Failing such determination, the number of
-- arbitrators is to be one."
@export How many arbitrators will hear my dispute (s 10)?
GIVEN `the number we agreed` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of arbitrators you and the other party agreed (0 if you did not agree one)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many arbitrators will there be` IS
    IF   `the number we agreed` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `the number we agreed`
    ELSE `the default number of arbitrators`

-- s 11(2): "The parties are free to agree on a procedure of appointing the arbitrator or arbitrators, subject to ... (4)".
-- s 11(3): "Failing such agreement -- (a) in an arbitration with 3 arbitrators and 2 parties, each party is to appoint one
-- arbitrator, and the 2 arbitrators so appointed are to appoint the third arbitrator; if a party fails to appoint the
-- arbitrator within 30 days of receipt of a request to do so from the other party, or if the 2 arbitrators fail to agree on
-- the third arbitrator within 30 days of their appointment, the appointment is to be made, on the request of a party, by
-- the Court; and (b) in an arbitration with a sole arbitrator, if the parties are unable to agree on the arbitrator, an
-- arbitrator is to be appointed, on the request of a party, by the Court; and (c) in an arbitration with 2, 4 or more
-- arbitrators or with 3 arbitrators and more than 2 parties, the appointment is to be made, at the request of a party, by
-- the Court."
-- s 11(4): under an agreed procedure, where "(a) a party fails to act ...; or (b) the parties, or 2 or more arbitrators, are
-- unable to reach an agreement ...; or (c) a third party, including an institution, fails to perform any function ...
-- any party may request the Court to take the necessary measure, unless the agreement on the appointment procedure provides
-- other means for securing the appointment."
-- "the Court" is the Supreme Court unless the agreement gives the District or Magistrates Court jurisdiction (s 6).
DECLARE `My appointment facts` HAS
    `we agreed an appointment procedure`                                   IS A BOOLEAN -- s 11(2)
    `under it a party failed to act, agreement failed, or an institution failed to act` IS A BOOLEAN -- s 11(4)(a)-(c)
    `the procedure provides other means of securing the appointment`       IS A BOOLEAN -- s 11(4)
    `the number of arbitrators`                                            IS A NUMBER  -- s 10
    `the number of parties`                                                IS A NUMBER  -- s 11(3)(a), (c)
    `we agree on the sole arbitrator`                                      IS A BOOLEAN -- s 11(3)(b)
    `days since the other party received my request to appoint, still not appointing` IS A NUMBER -- s 11(3)(a)
    `days since the two party arbitrators were appointed, still no third`  IS A NUMBER  -- s 11(3)(a)

DECLARE `Who appoints` IS ONE OF
    `as our agreed procedure provides`
    `the parties together, by agreement`
    `each party one, and those two the third`
    `the Court, at a party's request`

@export Who appoints the arbitrator in my arbitration (s 11)?
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `My appointment facts` @desc How the arbitrators are to be chosen, and what has happened so far
GIVETH A `Who appoints`
DECIDE `Who appoints the arbitrator` IS
    IF      `the facts`'s `we agreed an appointment procedure`
    THEN    IF       `the facts`'s `under it a party failed to act, agreement failed, or an institution failed to act`
                AND (NOT `the facts`'s `the procedure provides other means of securing the appointment`)
            THEN `the Court, at a party's request`
            ELSE `as our agreed procedure provides`
    ELSE BRANCH
            IF `the facts`'s `the number of arbitrators` EQUALS 1 AND `the facts`'s `we agree on the sole arbitrator`
                THEN `the parties together, by agreement`
            IF `the facts`'s `the number of arbitrators` EQUALS 1
                THEN `the Court, at a party's request`
            IF      `the facts`'s `the number of arbitrators` EQUALS 3
                AND `the facts`'s `the number of parties` EQUALS 2
                AND (    `the facts`'s `days since the other party received my request to appoint, still not appointing` GREATER THAN `the appointment period in days`
                      OR `the facts`'s `days since the two party arbitrators were appointed, still no third` GREATER THAN `the appointment period in days`)
                THEN `the Court, at a party's request`
            IF `the facts`'s `the number of arbitrators` EQUALS 3 AND `the facts`'s `the number of parties` EQUALS 2
                THEN `each party one, and those two the third`
            OTHERWISE `the Court, at a party's request`

§§ `12 -- may I challenge the arbitrator`

-- s 12(3): "An arbitrator may be challenged only if circumstances exist that give rise to justifiable doubts as to the
-- arbitrator's impartiality or independence, or if the arbitrator does not possess qualifications agreed to by the
-- parties."
-- s 12(4): "A party may challenge an arbitrator appointed by the party, or in whose appointment the party has participated,
-- only for reasons of which the party becomes aware after the appointment has been made."
-- s 12(6): "there are justifiable doubts ... only if there is a real danger of bias on the part of the arbitrator". Whether
-- there is a real danger of bias is for the tribunal or the Court (s 13); it is asked as a fact.
@export May I challenge the arbitrator (s 12(3), (4), (6))?
GIVEN `there is a real danger of bias on the arbitrator's part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is a real danger of bias (as the tribunal or Court would find)
      `the arbitrator lacks a qualification we agreed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the arbitrator lacks a qualification the parties agreed on
      `I appointed or took part in appointing the arbitrator` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you appointed the arbitrator or took part in the appointment
      `I learned the reason only after the appointment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you became aware of the reason only after the appointment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I challenge the arbitrator` IF
        (`there is a real danger of bias on the arbitrator's part` OR `the arbitrator lacks a qualification we agreed`)
    AND ((NOT `I appointed or took part in appointing the arbitrator`) OR `I learned the reason only after the appointment`)

§§ `18, 24 -- my right to be heard`

-- s 18: "The parties must be treated with equality and each party must be given a reasonable opportunity of presenting
-- the party's case."
-- s 24(2): "unless the parties have agreed that no hearings are to be held, the arbitral tribunal must hold such hearings at
-- an appropriate stage of the proceedings, if so requested by a party."
-- s 24(3): "The parties must be given sufficient advance notice of any hearing and of any meeting of the arbitral tribunal
-- for the purposes of inspection of goods, other property or documents."
-- s 24(4): "All statements, documents or other information supplied to the arbitral tribunal by one party must be
-- communicated to the other party."
-- s 24(5): "any expert report or evidentiary document on which the arbitral tribunal may rely in making its decision must be
-- communicated to the parties."
DECLARE `How I was heard` HAS
    `I was treated equally with the other party`                          IS A BOOLEAN -- s 18
    `I had a reasonable opportunity to present my case`                   IS A BOOLEAN -- s 18
    `I asked for an oral hearing`                                         IS A BOOLEAN -- s 24(2)
    `we agreed that no hearings would be held`                            IS A BOOLEAN -- s 24(2)
    `an oral hearing was held`                                            IS A BOOLEAN -- s 24(2)
    `I had sufficient advance notice of every hearing and inspection`     IS A BOOLEAN -- s 24(3)
    `everything the other party gave the tribunal was communicated to me` IS A BOOLEAN -- s 24(4)
    `every expert report or document the tribunal may rely on was communicated to me` IS A BOOLEAN -- s 24(5)

@export Must the tribunal hold an oral hearing if I ask for one (s 24(2))?
GIVEN `I asked for an oral hearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you asked the tribunal for an oral hearing
      `we agreed that no hearings would be held` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the parties agreed there would be no hearings
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the tribunal hold an oral hearing` IF
    `I asked for an oral hearing` AND (NOT `we agreed that no hearings would be held`)

@export Have I been denied the hearing the Act gives me (ss 18, 24)?
GIVEN `how` IS A `How I was heard` @desc How the arbitration treated you
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I been denied my right to be heard` IF
        (NOT `how`'s `I was treated equally with the other party`)
    OR  (NOT `how`'s `I had a reasonable opportunity to present my case`)
    OR  (    `Must the tribunal hold an oral hearing` (`how`'s `I asked for an oral hearing`) (`how`'s `we agreed that no hearings would be held`)
         AND (NOT `how`'s `an oral hearing was held`))
    OR  (NOT `how`'s `I had sufficient advance notice of every hearing and inspection`)
    OR  (NOT `how`'s `everything the other party gave the tribunal was communicated to me`)
    OR  (NOT `how`'s `every expert report or document the tribunal may rely on was communicated to me`)

§§ `27D, 30 -- a mediated settlement`

-- s 27D(1): "An arbitrator may act as a mediator in proceedings relating to a dispute between the parties to an
-- arbitration agreement (mediation proceedings) if -- (a) the arbitration agreement provides for the arbitrator to act as
-- mediator ...; or (b) each party has consented in writing to the arbitrator so acting."
-- s 27D(8): "mediator" includes "a conciliator or other non-arbitral intermediary".
@export May our arbitrator act as mediator in our dispute (s 27D(1))?
GIVEN `our arbitration agreement provides for the arbitrator to mediate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your arbitration agreement provides for the arbitrator to act as mediator
      `each party has consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every party has consented in writing to the arbitrator mediating
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May our arbitrator act as mediator` IF
    `our arbitration agreement provides for the arbitrator to mediate` OR `each party has consented in writing`

-- s 27D(4): "An arbitrator who has acted as mediator in mediation proceedings that are terminated may not conduct subsequent
-- arbitration proceedings in relation to the dispute without the written consent of all the parties to the arbitration
-- given on or after the termination of the mediation proceedings."
-- s 27D(5): if they consent, "no objection may be taken ... solely on the ground that he or she has acted previously as a
-- mediator". s 27D(6): if not, "the arbitrator's mandate is taken to have been terminated under section 14 and a
-- substitute arbitrator is to be appointed in accordance with section 15."
DECLARE `After the mediation` IS ONE OF
    `the same arbitrator may arbitrate, and I cannot object that they mediated`
    `a substitute arbitrator must be appointed`

@export May the arbitrator who mediated our dispute now arbitrate it (s 27D(4)-(6))?
GIVEN `every party consented in writing on or after the mediation ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether all parties gave written consent, after the mediation ended, to the arbitrator arbitrating
GIVETH A `After the mediation`
DECIDE `May the arbitrator who mediated now arbitrate` IS
    IF   `every party consented in writing on or after the mediation ended`
    THEN `the same arbitrator may arbitrate, and I cannot object that they mediated`
    ELSE `a substitute arbitrator must be appointed`

-- s 30(1): "If, during arbitral proceedings, the parties settle the dispute, the arbitral tribunal must terminate the
-- proceedings and, if requested by the parties and not objected to by the arbitral tribunal, record the settlement in the
-- form of an arbitral award on agreed terms." s 30(3): "Such an award has the same status and effect as any other award on
-- the merits of the case." s 35(1): an award "is to be recognised ... as binding and ... enforced".
-- A settlement reached outside arbitral proceedings (a mediation under the contract, a deed) is not an award; the Act says
-- nothing about enforcing it. It binds, if at all, as a contract or deed at general law (not this Act; not encoded).
DECLARE `How my settlement binds` IS ONE OF
    `as an arbitral award, enforceable under section 35`
    `the arbitration ends, and the settlement binds only as a contract or deed`
    `only as a contract or deed: this Act does not enforce it`

@export How is my settlement enforced (s 30, s 35)?
GIVEN `we settled during arbitral proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the dispute was settled while an arbitration was under way
      `the parties asked the tribunal to record it as an award` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the parties asked the tribunal to record the settlement as an award on agreed terms
      `the tribunal objected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the tribunal objected to recording it
GIVETH A `How my settlement binds`
DECIDE `How is my settlement enforced` IS
    IF      NOT `we settled during arbitral proceedings`
    THEN    `only as a contract or deed: this Act does not enforce it`
    ELSE IF `the parties asked the tribunal to record it as an award` AND (NOT `the tribunal objected`)
         THEN `as an arbitral award, enforceable under section 35`
         ELSE `the arbitration ends, and the settlement binds only as a contract or deed`

§§ `31, 33 -- the award`

-- s 31(3): "The award must state the reasons upon which it is based, unless the parties have agreed that no reasons are to
-- be given or the award is an award on agreed terms under section 30."
@export Must my award state its reasons (s 31(3))?
GIVEN `we agreed no reasons would be given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the parties agreed that no reasons are to be given
      `it is an award on agreed terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the award records a settlement under s 30
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my award state its reasons` IF
    (NOT `we agreed no reasons would be given`) AND (NOT `it is an award on agreed terms`)

-- s 33(1)(a): "Within 30 days of receipt of the award, unless another period of time has been agreed on by the parties ...
-- a party, with notice to the other party, may request the arbitral tribunal to correct in the award any errors in
-- computation, any clerical or typographical errors or any errors of similar nature".
@export Am I in time to ask the tribunal to correct my award (s 33(1))?
GIVEN `the date I received the award` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the award
      `the date of my request` IS A DATE @desc The day you send the request, with notice to the other party
      `another period we agreed, in days` IS A NUMBER @desc A different period the parties agreed (0 if none)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I in time to ask for a correction` IF
    IF   `another period we agreed, in days` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN Day `the date of my request` MINUS Day `the date I received the award` AT MOST `another period we agreed, in days`
    ELSE Day `the date of my request` MINUS Day `the date I received the award` AT MOST `the correction period in days`

§§ `34 -- can I have the award set aside`

-- s 34(1): "Recourse to the Court against an arbitral award may be made only by an application for setting aside in
-- accordance with subsections (2) and (3) or by an appeal under section 34A."
-- s 34(2): "An arbitral award may be set aside by the Court only if -- (a) the party making the application furnishes proof
-- that -- (i) a party to the arbitration agreement ... was under some incapacity, or the arbitration agreement is not valid
-- ...; or (ii) the party making the application was not given proper notice of the appointment of an arbitral tribunal or
-- of the arbitral proceedings or was otherwise unable to present the party's case; or (iii) the award deals with a dispute
-- not contemplated by or not falling within the terms of the submission to arbitration ... provided that, if the decisions
-- on matters submitted to arbitration can be separated from those not so submitted, only that part of the award which
-- contains decisions on matters not submitted to arbitration may be set aside; or (iv) the composition of the arbitral
-- tribunal or the arbitral procedure was not in accordance with the agreement of the parties ... or, failing such
-- agreement, was not in accordance with this Act; or (b) the Court finds that -- (i) the subject matter of the dispute is
-- not capable of settlement by arbitration under the law of this State; or (ii) the award is in conflict with the public
-- policy of this State."
-- s 34(3): "An application for setting aside may not be made after 3 months have elapsed from the date on which the party
-- making that application had received the award or, if a request had been made under section 33, from the date on which
-- that request had been disposed of by the arbitral tribunal."
-- "may be set aside": the Court has a discretion even where a ground is proved; the outcome says "may".
DECLARE `My setting-aside application` HAS
    `I prove a party lacked capacity or the agreement is invalid`         IS A BOOLEAN -- s 34(2)(a)(i)
    `I prove I had no proper notice or could not present my case`         IS A BOOLEAN -- s 34(2)(a)(ii)
    `I prove the award goes beyond the submission to arbitration`         IS A BOOLEAN -- s 34(2)(a)(iii)
    `the part beyond the submission can be separated`                     IS A BOOLEAN -- s 34(2)(a)(iii) proviso
    `I prove the tribunal or procedure departed from our agreement or the Act` IS A BOOLEAN -- s 34(2)(a)(iv)
    `the Court finds the dispute not capable of settlement by arbitration` IS A BOOLEAN -- s 34(2)(b)(i)
    `the Court finds the award against the public policy of Western Australia` IS A BOOLEAN -- s 34(2)(b)(ii)
    `the date I received the award`                                       IS A DATE    -- s 34(3)
    `a section 33 request was made`                                       IS A BOOLEAN -- s 34(3)
    `the date the tribunal disposed of it`                                IS A DATE    -- s 34(3)
    `the date I apply`                                                    IS A DATE    -- s 34(3)

DECLARE `Setting aside` IS ONE OF
    `the Court may set aside the award`
    `the Court may set aside only the part beyond the submission`
    `no ground: the award stands`
    `too late: 3 months have passed`

@export Am I in time to apply to set aside my award (s 34(3))?
GIVEN `the application` IS A `My setting-aside application` @desc Your application and its dates
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I in time to apply to set aside the award` IF
    `within 3 months of the award` (`the application`'s `the date I received the award`) (`the application`'s `a section 33 request was made`) (`the application`'s `the date the tribunal disposed of it`) (`the application`'s `the date I apply`)

@export Can I have my award set aside, and how much of it (s 34)?
GIVEN `the application` IS A `My setting-aside application` @desc Your application, its grounds and its dates
GIVETH A `Setting aside`
DECIDE `Can I have my award set aside` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `Am I in time to apply to set aside the award` `the application`
            THEN `too late: 3 months have passed`
        IF     `the application`'s `I prove a party lacked capacity or the agreement is invalid`
            OR `the application`'s `I prove I had no proper notice or could not present my case`
            OR `the application`'s `I prove the tribunal or procedure departed from our agreement or the Act`
            OR `the application`'s `the Court finds the dispute not capable of settlement by arbitration`
            OR `the application`'s `the Court finds the award against the public policy of Western Australia`
            OR (`the application`'s `I prove the award goes beyond the submission to arbitration` AND (NOT `the application`'s `the part beyond the submission can be separated`))
            THEN `the Court may set aside the award`
        IF `the application`'s `I prove the award goes beyond the submission to arbitration`
            THEN `the Court may set aside only the part beyond the submission`
        OTHERWISE `no ground: the award stands`

§§ `34A -- can I appeal on a question of law`

-- s 34A(1): "An appeal lies to the Court on a question of law arising out of an award if -- (a) the parties agree, before
-- the end of the appeal period referred to in subsection (6), that an appeal may be made under this section; and (b) the
-- Court grants leave."
-- s 34A(3): "The Court must not grant leave unless it is satisfied -- (a) that the determination of the question will
-- substantially affect the rights of one or more of the parties; and (b) that the question is one which the arbitral
-- tribunal was asked to determine; and (c) that, on the basis of the findings of fact in the award -- (i) the decision of
-- the tribunal on the question is obviously wrong; or (ii) the question is one of general public importance and the
-- decision of the tribunal is at least open to serious doubt; and (d) that, despite the agreement of the parties to resolve
-- the matter by arbitration, it is just and proper in all the circumstances for the Court to determine the question."
-- s 34A(6): "An appeal may not be made under this section after 3 months have elapsed from the date on which the party
-- making the appeal received the award or, if a request had been made under section 33, from the date on which that
-- request had been disposed of".
-- Leave is still discretionary when s 34A(3) is satisfied ("must not grant leave unless"), so the best outcome is "if the
-- Court grants leave".
DECLARE `My appeal` HAS
    `it is a question of law arising out of the award`                    IS A BOOLEAN -- s 34A(1)
    `the parties agreed to an appeal before the appeal period ended`      IS A BOOLEAN -- s 34A(1)(a)
    `the Court is satisfied it will substantially affect a party's rights` IS A BOOLEAN -- s 34A(3)(a)
    `the Court is satisfied the tribunal was asked to decide it`          IS A BOOLEAN -- s 34A(3)(b)
    `the Court is satisfied the decision is obviously wrong`              IS A BOOLEAN -- s 34A(3)(c)(i)
    `the Court is satisfied it is of general public importance and the decision open to serious doubt` IS A BOOLEAN -- s 34A(3)(c)(ii)
    `the Court is satisfied it is just and proper for the Court to decide it` IS A BOOLEAN -- s 34A(3)(d)
    `the date I received the award`                                       IS A DATE    -- s 34A(6)
    `a section 33 request was made`                                       IS A BOOLEAN -- s 34A(6)
    `the date the tribunal disposed of it`                                IS A DATE    -- s 34A(6)
    `the date I appeal`                                                   IS A DATE    -- s 34A(6)

DECLARE `Appeal` IS ONE OF
    `no appeal: only a question of law may be appealed`
    `no appeal: the parties have not agreed to one`
    `too late: the appeal period has ended`
    `no appeal: the Court must not grant leave`
    `an appeal lies if the Court grants leave`

@export May the Court grant me leave to appeal (s 34A(3))?
GIVEN `the appeal` IS A `My appeal` @desc Your proposed appeal and what the Court is satisfied of
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Court grant leave to appeal` IF
        `the appeal`'s `the Court is satisfied it will substantially affect a party's rights`
    AND `the appeal`'s `the Court is satisfied the tribunal was asked to decide it`
    AND (    `the appeal`'s `the Court is satisfied the decision is obviously wrong`
          OR `the appeal`'s `the Court is satisfied it is of general public importance and the decision open to serious doubt`)
    AND `the appeal`'s `the Court is satisfied it is just and proper for the Court to decide it`

@export Can I appeal against my award on a question of law (s 34A)?
GIVEN `the appeal` IS A `My appeal` @desc Your proposed appeal, the parties' agreement, and its dates
GIVETH A `Appeal`
DECIDE `Can I appeal against my award` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the appeal`'s `it is a question of law arising out of the award`
            THEN `no appeal: only a question of law may be appealed`
        IF NOT `the appeal`'s `the parties agreed to an appeal before the appeal period ended`
            THEN `no appeal: the parties have not agreed to one`
        IF NOT `within 3 months of the award` (`the appeal`'s `the date I received the award`) (`the appeal`'s `a section 33 request was made`) (`the appeal`'s `the date the tribunal disposed of it`) (`the appeal`'s `the date I appeal`)
            THEN `too late: the appeal period has ended`
        IF NOT `May the Court grant leave to appeal` `the appeal`
            THEN `no appeal: the Court must not grant leave`
        OTHERWISE `an appeal lies if the Court grants leave`

§§ `35, 36 -- recognition and enforcement`

-- s 35(1): "An arbitral award, irrespective of the State or Territory in which it was made, is to be recognised in this
-- State as binding and, on application in writing to the Court, is to be enforced subject to the provisions of this section
-- and section 36." s 35(2): "The party relying on an award or applying for its enforcement must supply the original award
-- or a copy of the original award."
-- s 36(1): "Recognition or enforcement ... may be refused only -- (a) at the request of the party against whom it is
-- invoked, if that party furnishes to the Court proof that -- (i) ... incapacity ... or the arbitration agreement is not
-- valid ...; or (ii) the party against whom the award is invoked was not given proper notice ... or was otherwise unable to
-- present the party's case; or (iii) the award deals with a dispute not ... within the terms of the submission ...; or
-- (iv) the composition of the arbitral tribunal or the arbitral procedure was not in accordance with the agreement ...; or
-- (v) the award has not yet become binding on the parties or has been set aside or suspended by a court ...; or (b) if the
-- Court finds that -- (i) the subject matter ... is not capable of settlement by arbitration under the law of this State; or
-- (ii) the recognition or enforcement of the award would be contrary to the public policy of this State."
-- s 36(1)(a) is grouped as one fact; s 36(1)(a)(iii)'s severance proviso is not encoded.
@export Will the Court enforce my award (ss 35, 36)?
GIVEN `I apply to the Court in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have applied in writing to the Court for enforcement
      `I supply the original award or a copy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you supply the original award or a copy of it
      `the other party proves a ground in section 36(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the party you enforce against proves incapacity or invalidity, lack of notice, excess of submission, irregular tribunal or procedure, or that the award is not binding, set aside or suspended
      `the Court finds the dispute not arbitrable or enforcement against public policy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Court's own finding under s 36(1)(b) (asked, not guessed)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will the Court enforce my award` IF
        `I apply to the Court in writing`
    AND `I supply the original award or a copy`
    AND (NOT `the other party proves a ground in section 36(1)(a)`)
    AND (NOT `the Court finds the dispute not arbitrable or enforcement against public policy`)

@export Can I resist enforcement of the award against me (s 36(1))?
GIVEN `I prove a ground in section 36(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can prove one of the grounds in s 36(1)(a)(i)-(v)
      `the Court finds the dispute not arbitrable or enforcement against public policy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Court's own finding under s 36(1)(b) (asked, not guessed)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I resist enforcement of the award` IF
    `I prove a ground in section 36(1)(a)` OR `the Court finds the dispute not arbitrable or enforcement against public policy`
